#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:134
msgid "Document Search"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:134
msgid "A search box that sends visitors to a library page with their search applied."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:135
#: includes/Admin/Settings/Viewer.php:16
#: includes/Integrations/Elementor/ViewerWidget.php:18
msgid "PDF Viewer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:135
msgid "Show a PDF from a document, the Media Library or a URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:136
msgid "Save as PDF"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:136
msgid "The Post to PDF button, placed where you want it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:137
msgid "Block"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:137
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:138
msgid "Elementor users get four widgets with the same options: Document Library, Document List, Document Download and PDF Viewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:139
msgid "Other page builders (Divi, Bricks, Beaver Builder, WPBakery, Oxygen, Breakdance): add a shortcode or text module with <code>[document_engine_library]</code>, <code>[document_engine_search]</code>, <code>[document_engine_documents]</code>, <code>[document_engine_document id=\"123\"]</code> or <code>[document_engine_viewer id=\"123\"]</code>. All options of the blocks are available as shortcode attributes (see the shortcode reference)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:141
msgid "Document lists and related documents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:142
msgid "The Document List block and <code>[document_engine_documents]</code> show a few documents in a compact list: newest, recently updated, most downloaded, or related to a document (sharing its categories or tags)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:143
msgid "Settings → Documents → <strong>Related documents</strong> adds a related list under each document page automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:145
msgid "Search box for your header or sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:146
msgid "The Document Search block (or <code>[document_engine_search page=\"123\"]</code>) shows a search field anywhere. Choose the page that holds your library; searches land there with results already filtered. If you do not choose one, it uses the first published page with a Document Library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:148
msgid "QR codes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:149
msgid "Every published document has a QR code in the editor sidebar (Document file panel → QR code → Show). Download it as PNG or SVG for printed notices, posters or meeting packs. The code points to the document's page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:151
#: includes/Admin/Settings/PDF.php:22
msgid "Post to PDF"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:152
msgid "Adds a \"Download PDF\" button to posts, pages or other post types that turns the content into a PDF, generated on your server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:154
msgid "Choose where the button appears in Settings → Post to PDF → Button (post types, text, placement, alignment, download or open)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:155
msgid "Header and footer (logo, title, page numbers), paper size (A4, US Letter, US Legal, A5 or A3), orientation, margins and text size, theme styles or custom CSS. Sites in a right-to-left language get right-to-left PDFs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:156
msgid "Fonts: Sans, Serif or Monospaced (DejaVu, covering Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic and Hebrew), or your own .ttf/.otf font from the Media Library, for all text or only for characters the main font lacks (for example Chinese, Japanese or Korean)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:157
msgid "Protection: optionally stop readers printing, copying or editing the PDF (PDF permissions)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:158
msgid "Document Engine Pro adds text and image watermarks, with placeholders such as {name} and {date}, and Handbook PDFs that combine many posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:159
msgid "Content shortcodes: <code>[document_engine_pdf_remove]</code> hides content from the PDF, <code>[document_engine_pdf_page_break]</code> starts a new page, <code>[document_engine_pdf_columns]</code> and <code>[document_engine_pdf_column_break]</code> lay out columns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:161
msgid "PDFs are made only for published, public posts of the post types you ticked (or posts containing a Save as PDF block), never for private or password-protected posts. Images from internal network addresses are left out. Generated PDFs are cached, and each visitor can create a limited number per minute (Settings → Advanced → Performance)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:164
msgid "When switched on (Settings → Documents → Accessibility → Format requests), document pages show a \"Need this in another format?\" link. Visitors choose a format (for example large print or plain text), leave their name and email, and the request is emailed to you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:165
msgid "Requests are listed under Documents → Reports → Format requests, with a count of open requests. Reply to the email with the alternative version, then mark the request done. Only editors and administrators can see requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:166
msgid "The form has spam protection (a time check, a hidden field and limits per visitor, per document and per day). Requests contain names and emails; they are included in WordPress's personal data export and erase tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:168
#: includes/Admin/Migrate.php:33
#: includes/Admin/Migrate.php:93
msgid "Migrate from another plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:169
msgid "Documents → Tools → Migrate copies documents from Download Monitor, WordPress Download Manager, Barn2 Document Library, Simple Download Monitor and Simple File List into Document Engine: titles, descriptions, categories, tags, files, download counts and dates. Simple File List folders become nested categories."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:170
msgid "Simple File List was closed on WordPress.org in July 2026 for a security issue. Migrating copies its files into the Media Library; after checking the result, deactivate and delete Simple File List. Pages with [eeSFL] (including showfolder=\"…\") keep working and show the matching documents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:172
msgid "Run a preview first: it shows how many items will be copied and flags locked items (paid, email- or captcha-gated) that need attention."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:173
msgid "The original plugin's data is not changed. Running it again skips items already copied."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:174
msgid "The old plugin's shortcodes keep working and its download links redirect to the new documents, so you can deactivate it afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:175
msgid "Members-only items become drafts in the free plugin (Pro moves their files to private storage and applies the access rule)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:178
msgid "Command palette and AI agents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:179
msgid "Press Ctrl/Cmd+K anywhere in the admin to add a document, open the library, dashboard or settings, or jump to a document by typing its title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:180
msgid "On WordPress 6.9+, the plugin registers two read-only abilities (Abilities API): search documents and get a document. AI assistants connected to your site (for example through the MCP adapter) can use them; they only ever return documents the signed-in user may open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:182
msgid "Who can manage documents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:183
msgid "Documents have their own permissions, separate from posts. In Settings → Advanced → Permissions choose which roles:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:185
msgid "<strong>Manage all documents</strong> (default: Administrator, Editor): edit and publish any document, manage categories, see requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:186
msgid "<strong>Publish their own documents</strong> (default: Author)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:187
msgid "<strong>Draft their own documents</strong> (default: Contributor): an editor publishes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:189
msgid "Settings and migration need the Administrator's \"manage options\" permission."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:195
msgid "Pro features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:197
msgid "What the Pro add-on adds, and where to find it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:199
msgid "Install Pro and activate your licence"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:201
msgid "Buy Pro, then either download the Pro ZIP from your account and upload it under Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin, or enter your licence key at the bottom of Documents → Free vs Pro to install it in one step."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:202
msgid "Keep the free plugin active; Pro builds on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:203
msgid "Enter the licence key in Documents → Settings → License. An active licence gives you updates from the Plugins screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:205
msgid "Deactivating Pro returns the site to the free features. Pro data (access rules, logs, acknowledgements) stays in the database unless you delete it on uninstall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:207
msgid "Access control and private files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:208
msgid "Decide who can open each document: everyone, logged-in users, users with chosen roles, named people, or members of Paid Memberships Pro levels and WooCommerce Memberships plans. Set it per document (Access & security panel) or for a whole category (on the category screen); documents follow their categories unless they have their own rule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:209
msgid "Membership plugins: with Paid Memberships Pro or WooCommerce Memberships active, pick their levels or plans directly (\"Members of these membership levels\"). Plugins that give members a WordPress role, such as MemberPress and Restrict Content Pro, work with \"Users with these roles\". If the membership plugin is switched off, documents limited to its levels stay closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:211
msgid "Restricted documents are shown with a lock, or hidden from people who cannot open them (Settings → Access & Pro → Access)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:212
msgid "<strong>Protected storage</strong>: files of restricted documents move to a private uploads folder, so the file address alone cannot be used to download them. A Site Health test checks that the folder really is private."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:213
msgid "Logged-out visitors are asked to log in; logged-in people without access see a clear message."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:214
msgid "Restricted documents are left out of site search, feeds, library results (when set to hide) and file-content search for people who cannot open them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:215
msgid "<strong>Cloud storage</strong>: files stay on your server. If a media offload plugin (WP Offload Media, Media Cloud, Infinite Uploads…) copies uploads to a bucket, exclude the protected documents folder from offloading; Site Health warns you when one is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:218
msgid "Share links"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:219
msgid "Give someone without an account access to one document for a limited time (Access & security panel → Share link). Name the link after the recipient to see when they opened it; optionally get an email on the first open. Revoke a link at any time. Links default to Settings → Access & Pro → Share links last (7 days)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:220
msgid "<strong>Uses allowed</strong>: limit a named link to one use (single use), 3, 5 or 10. Each download, or each time the document is opened in the viewer, is one use; after the last one the link stops working. The editor shows how many uses are left."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:222
msgid "Secure viewer and stamped downloads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:223
msgid "Secure mode shows a PDF in the viewer only: no download, print or copy buttons, and each page carries a watermark with the reader's name, email and date (pattern in Settings → Access & Pro → Secure viewer). Downloads of secure documents are blocked. Only PDFs can be shown in secure mode; other secure files can be neither viewed nor downloaded. Optionally, downloaded PDFs of other documents can be stamped with the reader's details."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:224
msgid "A watermark discourages sharing and identifies leaks; no viewer can stop a determined person photographing a screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:226
msgid "Email gate and leads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:227
msgid "Ask for a name and email (and optionally organization) before a download, with your consent text. Switch it on per document or for all documents. Logged-in users and visitors who already filled the form (for a number of days) go straight through. Leads are listed under Reports → Leads, can be exported, sent to a webhook or emailed to you, and deleted after a retention period."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:229
msgid "Accept terms before opening"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:230
msgid "Ask everyone, logged in or not, to tick \"I agree\" to your terms (a licence, disclaimer, embargo or confidentiality notice) before a document opens. Switch it on per document (Access & security → Accept terms) or for all documents, and set the heading, the terms and the checkbox text in Settings → Access & Pro → Email gate & terms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:232
msgid "The document page shows the terms instead of the viewer until they are accepted; direct file links go to the same form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:233
msgid "Each acceptance is recorded in the activity log (\"Accepted terms\") with the person or visitor and the date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:234
msgid "Acceptance is remembered per document. Changing the wording of the terms asks everyone again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:235
msgid "Editors who can edit the document are never asked. With an email gate too, visitors give their details first, then accept the terms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:238
msgid "Office previews (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:239
msgid "Switch on Settings → Access & Pro → Office previews to show Word, Excel and PowerPoint files on their document page and in the preview popup, using Microsoft's free Office Online viewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:240
msgid "Microsoft downloads the file from your site to display it, so only documents anyone may open are previewed: restricted, secure-viewer, email-gate and terms documents never are. Files up to 10 MB (Word, PowerPoint) or 5 MB (Excel). Your site must be reachable from the internet, so previews don't appear on local or staging sites. Mention Microsoft in your privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:242
msgid "Activity, reading analytics and searches"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:244
msgid "<strong>Reports → Activity</strong>: views, downloads, blocked attempts, leads and share-link opens, with a chart, top documents and a filterable audit log (CSV export)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:245
msgid "<strong>Reading analytics</strong>: for PDFs in the viewer, how long people spend on each page and how far they read. Filter the Activity page to one document to see it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:246
msgid "<strong>Reports → Searches</strong>: what visitors search for in libraries, and which searches found nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:247
msgid "The documents list shows views in the last 30 days next to downloads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:249
msgid "No IP addresses are stored in these logs: visitors who are not logged in are identified by a hash that changes daily. Entries older than the retention period (default 365 days) are deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:251
msgid "Versions, review and expiry dates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:253
msgid "Replace a document's file and the old one is kept in its version history; links do not change. Restore any version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:254
msgid "From the documents list, use the \"Upload new version\" row action, or drop a file onto a row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:255
msgid "Give documents a review-by date and an expiry date. Expired documents are unpublished automatically; a daily email lists documents due for review."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:258
msgid "Read and confirm (acknowledgements)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:259
msgid "Ask people to confirm they have read a document (\"I have read and understood…\"). In the document's <strong>Read & confirm</strong> panel, choose the roles who must confirm and a deadline; they see it on the document page and in the Required Reading block. Reports → Acknowledgements shows who has and has not confirmed, sends reminders, and exports evidence (name, time, statement, a fingerprint of the file)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:260
msgid "After an important change, start a new round from the Acknowledgements screen so everyone confirms again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:262
msgid "Notifications, webhooks and subscriptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:264
msgid "Signed webhooks for events such as document published, new version, acknowledged, submitted and new lead. The <code>X-DocumentEngine-Signature</code> header is <code>sha256=</code> followed by the HMAC-SHA256 of the timestamp header, a full stop and the raw body (<code>timestamp.body</code>), keyed with the signing secret."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:265
msgid "Posts to a Slack or Microsoft Teams channel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:266
msgid "Email subscriptions: logged-in people follow categories (Subscribe block) and get an email when a document is published there, with one-click unsubscribe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:269
msgid "Front-end submissions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:270
msgid "The Submit Document block lets chosen roles upload documents from the front end. Submissions are saved as pending (or published) with allowed file types and a size limit (Settings → Access & Pro → Review & submissions)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:272
msgid "Bulk and CSV import"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:273
msgid "Documents → Tools → Import: drop many files at once to create one document per file, or import a CSV spreadsheet (title, file_url or attachment_id, category, tags, description, status, id, and cf:key columns for custom fields). Rows with an id update that document. Also available as <code>wp dengine import</code>."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:275
msgid "Custom fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:276
msgid "Settings → Fields: add your own details to documents, such as a reference number, department or review date. Types: text, long text, number, date, choice list, yes/no, link, email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:278
msgid "Edit them in the document sidebar's Details panel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:279
msgid "Show them as library columns, filters (with counts) and sort options, on document pages, and in search."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:280
msgid "Import them from CSV with <code>cf:key</code> columns (write \"-\" to clear a value)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:281
msgid "Use fields you already have in Advanced Custom Fields (ACF): add them from the Fields tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:284
msgid "My documents, required reading and handbooks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:286
msgid "<strong>My Documents</strong> block: a client or staff area listing the documents shared with the logged-in person, with \"New\" since their last visit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:287
msgid "<strong>Required Reading</strong> block: each person's documents to confirm, with deadlines."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:288
msgid "<strong>Handbook PDF</strong> (Documents → Tools → Handbook PDF, or <code>[document_engine_handbook]</code>): many posts in one PDF with a cover page and table of contents."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:289
msgid "<strong>ZIP download</strong>: a Select column in table libraries lets visitors download several documents as one ZIP (up to 100 files and 250 MB; needs the PHP zip extension)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:292
msgid "AI assistant and file-content search"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:293
msgid "Search finds words inside PDF, Word (.docx), Excel (.xlsx), PowerPoint (.pptx), OpenDocument and plain text files up to 30 MB, in libraries and site search. Older .doc, .xls and .ppt files and files linked from other sites are not indexed. The AI assistant (Suggest details, in the editor's AI assistant panel) proposes a title, a short summary, categories and tags from the file's text for you to review. It needs an AI provider connected in WordPress (Settings → Connectors, WordPress 7.0 or newer); Pro holds no keys of its own. Restricted, private and password-protected documents are not sent to AI unless you allow it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:295
#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:347
msgid "Abuse protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:296
msgid "Limit how many different documents one person can download or view per day (ZIP downloads included), and add Cloudflare Turnstile to the email gate, format request and submission forms (Settings → Access & Pro → Abuse protection)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:298
msgid "WP-CLI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:305
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocsContent.php:307
